---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Navy Visual Style Guide | Jonathan Wideman"
	description="A guide that explains how and why Navy commands should communicate, visually and verbally, across social platforms."
>
	<main>
		<p class="back"><a href="/#projects">← Back to projects</a></p>

		<h1>Navy Visual Style Guide</h1>

		<p>
			Across the fleet, commands were branding Navy content their own way, with ship crests, custom
			logos and local styles. The result didn't look like it came from the Navy. It could have been
			any military influencer, while the other branches kept their branding tight.
		</p>

		<p>
			I built a guide that explains how and why Navy commands should communicate, visually and
			verbally, across social platforms. It set one color palette, fixed which logo marks to use and
			when, and laid out typefaces and how to rank them.
		</p>

		<p>
			Public affairs shops around the world now use it to stay on brand. Content now flows between
			the Navy's flagship accounts and local commands without reworking it to fit.
		</p>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	main {
		max-width: 42rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 1.5rem 0 3rem;
	}

	.back {
		margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
		font-size: 0.9375rem;
	}

	h1 {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		font-size: 2.25rem;
		line-height: 1.2;
	}
</style>
